#X obj 667 11 env.tscale;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 286 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 Scales the timing of an envelope: multiplies all time
values of the envelope by the given scale factor. A factor of 1 leaves
the envelope unchanged \, values less than 1 make it shorter \, values
greater than 1 make it longer. The shape of the envelope (its values)
is not affected — only its duration.;
#X text 240 184 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 209 • Tempo-relative envelopes — scaling an envelope so
that its duration matches the current tempo or note length \, for example
making a short envelope for staccato and a long one for legato from
the same base shape.;
#X text 250 279 • Real-time duration control — changing the overall
length of an envelope in real time by linking the scale to a knob \,
a slider \, or a performance parameter such as key velocity.;
#X msg 50 412 ar 20 30 \, bang;
